coder › Done and handed off to architect.

**Changed:**
- `src/queue.ts` — replaced the `#pending` array / `Promise.all` capture with a promise-chain tail. `push` chains `this.#tail.then(() => job())`, so a job never starts synchronously inside `push` and runs strictly after the previous one; the rejection handler records the error and returns `undefined` so the tail always resolves. `drain` loops, re-reading `#tail` after each `await`, returning only when the tail it awaited is still the current one — so jobs pushed while draining are awaited. Kept `readonly errors: Error[] = []`.
- `src/queue.test.ts` — kept `drain waits for every job`, added: serial order test (3 jobs, staggered `setTimeout` delays; asserts start order, finish order, and max concurrent running = 1), push-not-synchronous test, throwing job (error recorded with message `'boom'`, later job still runs), non-Error rejection wrapped into `Error('nope')`, and drain-waits-for-jobs-pushed-mid-drain test.

